@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@
+# Long-context decode attention on SM120 (branch `dsv41-attn-longctx`)
+
+Scope: the decode step's context-dependent cost on the 1M cc3 config (deployed
+stack at fc0beb9: GEMV + FP8 head + FP8 wo_a + fusion + PDL_ALL + pinned Engram +
+fused top-k slots). Baseline profiles `v41/profile/attn_base.{1..8}` (nsys,
+both TP ranks in one file; per-rank numbers below divide by 2 x steps).
+
+## Where the context-dependent time is (baseline, per rank, per decode step)
+
+| prompt | step growth vs 8K | topk_transform (v1) | dense mqa logits (replay) | paged mqa logits | sparse-MLA decode | elementwise growth |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 8K | 0 | 0.01 ms | 0 | 0.007 | 0.27 | 0 |
+| 128K | +0.26 ms | 0.12 (4 x 31 us) | 0.04 | 0.03 | 0.28 | +0.05 |
+| 256K | +0.45 ms | 0.22 (4 x 55 us) | 0.08 | 0.05 | 0.28 | +0.07 |
+| 512K | +0.78 ms | 0.39 (4 x 100 us) | 0.17 (2.06 ms every 5th step) | 0.08 | 0.28 | +0.10 |
+
+Sparse-MLA decode is flat with context (fixed selected pages). The growth is the
+indexer: the decode top-k over the compressed score row and the bounded-replay
+tail's dense scoring. cc3 (attn_base.7/8) shows the same per-rank kernel costs.
+
+## Finding 1: top-k v2 (8-block clusters + DSMEM) works on SM120 and was disabled by mistake
+
+`srt/arg_groups/model_hook.py` disabled `SGLANG_OPT_USE_TOPK_V2` on SM120 with
+the rationale "requires >99KB SMEM". Measured on the RTX PRO 6000 (cc 12.0, CUDA
+13.0.3): `cudaOccupancyMaxActiveClusters` for an 8-block cluster = 46, DSMEM
+`map_shared_rank` reads correct, the v2 module (`sgl_kernel_jit_dpsk_v4_topk_v2`)
+compiles and runs, static smem ~27 KB (`enable_smem_spilling` is a PTX pragma, not
+an attribute). `kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_topk_v2_sm120.py` (v1 vs v2, bs 1/3,
+L 4K..256K, random / heavily tied / -inf tails): selected sets identical in every
+case (ties resolved to the same score multiset), timing per call on an idle GPU:
+
+| L | v1 (1 block) | v2 | speedup |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 4096 | 5.4 us | 3.1 us | 1.7x |
+| 20000 | 11.3 | 5.1 | 2.2x |
+| 65536 | 20.6 | 7.8 | 2.6x |
+| 131072 | 36.3 | 9.3 | 3.9x |
+| 262144 | 63.6 | 11.0 | 5.8x |
+
+Change: the hook now honours an explicit `SGLANG_OPT_USE_TOPK_V2` setting on SM120
+(default still off there); lanes opt in with `-e SGLANG_OPT_USE_TOPK_V2=1`. The
+decode dispatch (`_low_ratio_index_topk_decode`, `indexer.py`) needs no change:
+`raw_indices` is None at decode, so v2 is taken for every low-ratio layer.
+
+## Finding 2: the bounded-replay dense scoring ran on one SM
+
+`sm120_fp4_mqa_logits` (DeepGEMM) schedules persistent blocks over q blocks of 4
+rows and streams every KV block of a q block's window inside that block. The
+replay tail is <= 16 rows against the whole window, so one SM streams 128K-512K
+keys: 2.06 ms per call at 512K (0.2 calls per step per layer). The kernel stores
+`logits[row, kv - ks[row]]` under its own `[ks, ke)` guard, so rows may be
+replicated per KV chunk: `_dense_fp4_mqa_logits_kv_split` replicates rows once per
+8192-column chunk (rows sharing a window start and chunk share a q block, so no
+block streams beyond its chunk), calls the kernel once, and gathers the chunk
+outputs back to `[rows, width]`. Bitwise equal to the direct call on every valid
+column (`kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_dense_indexer_kv_split.py`, rows 1..16, L
+20K..400K, single and two-request windows). Flags:
+`SGLANG_DSV41_DENSE_INDEXER_KV_SPLIT=1`, `_KV_CHUNK` (8192), `_MAX_ROWS` (16).
+
+## Measurements (`v41/profile/ab_attn.log`, frozen 01:57-02:16, 1M cc3 config, arms booted from this worktree)
+
+Microbenchmarks with the GPU idle (server down): the top-k table above; the
+KV-split dense scoring at L=400K, rows 1-7: direct 4.19 ms -> split 0.29 ms
+(14x); ragged two-request rows 0.30 ms after grouping by window start (the
+ungrouped first version streamed union windows and took 1.6 ms).
+
+In situ, bench_v41 single-stream, 256 new tokens; round 0 prefills the prompt and
+round 1 hits the prefix cache, so round 1 is the decode number. Arm A ran cold
+(first JIT/autotune after boot: P=512 at 60-66 tok/s vs A2 109-138), so the
+usable baseline is A2:
+
+| prompt tokens | A2 baseline | B (v2 top-k + KV split) | delta |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 512, cc1 | 137.9 tok/s | 140.5 | +1.9% |
+| 131072, cc1 | 116.7 | 118.8 | +1.8% |
+| 262144, cc1 | 104.2 | 108.7 | +4.3% (9.6 -> 9.2 ms/step) |
+| 131072, cc3 | 228.3 | 233.7 | +2.4% |
+
+Predicted saving at 256K per step: top-k 4 x (55 -> ~11 us) = 0.18 ms plus the
+replay dense scoring 0.08 -> ~0.01 ms amortised = ~0.25 ms; measured 0.4 ms
+(single runs, ~2% noise band). Prefill unchanged (131K prompt: 11.1 s both).
+GSM8K-100 nothink 99.0%, GSM8K-20 think 19/20 (parity); needle recall PASS at
+195,700 and 430,492 prompt tokens. Winner B was booted and the benchmark
+unfrozen at 02:16 with `SGLANG_OPT_USE_TOPK_V2=1 SGLANG_DSV41_DENSE_INDEXER_KV_SPLIT=1`
+on top of the fc0beb9 stack, from this worktree.
+
+## What remains on the attention side
+
+- The score masking chain in `two_level_decode_logits` (reachable + published
+  masks, ~0.1 ms per step at 512K) could move into the top-k kernel.
+- The DeepGEMM dense kernel's host-side cost (~0.3 ms per call even at 20K
+  columns: TMA descriptor encoding and wrapper ops) bounds the replay path now.
+- Sparse-MLA decode is flat (0.28 ms per step) and not context-dependent.
+- Not done: an nsys per-kernel breakdown of the deployed B server at long
+  context (would need another freeze); the in-situ gain is inferred from the
+  bench delta and the idle-GPU microbenchmarks.
