@@ -0,0 +1,146 @@
+# Pinned in-RAM engram tables with in-graph gather (branch `dsv41-engram-pinned`)
+
+Target: the last host-side work in the captured decode step on the 1M cc3 config. After launch
+fusion (`NOTES-launch-fusion.md`) the disk-backed pre-gather still costs, per step and rank, one
+stream sync (`hash_ids.to("cpu")`), a host dedupe, an `index_select` into pinned staging, one H2D
+and one gather launch per engram layer: ~289 µs of host time plus the eager pre-replay launches,
+and the step cannot run as one uninterrupted graph replay.
+
+## Layout facts (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, verified against config.json and the disk tables)
+
+- Two engram layers (1 and 14), 384,006,168 and 384,016,682 rows each; a row is one head's
+  256-dim fp8 e4m3 payload plus 2 e8m0 block scales (128-wide blocks) = 264 bytes; a table is
+  101,377,628,352 bytes (94.4 GiB). 24 ids per token per layer ((max_ngram 4 − 1) × 8 heads):
+  6.3 KB per token per layer, 72 rows at M = 3.
+- Every TP rank reads the whole table in the shared layout (no all-reduce), so both ranks map
+  the same memfd; the load-time fill is rank-sharded by byte range.
+
+## Why "copy", not "register"
+
+`cudaHostRegister` on the ext4-backed `MAP_SHARED` or `MAP_PRIVATE` mapping returns
+`cudaErrorInvalidValue` (get_user_pages refuses FOLL_LONGTERM pins of file-backed, non-shmem
+pages), measured with a 512 MiB file (`scratchpad/engram-test/reg_test.py`). A memfd (shmem)
+registers fine. `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED=register` is kept and fails loud with the driver
+error, so the limitation is a test, not folklore.
+
+## What was built (commit c711f5c)
+
+- `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED=copy`: shared memfd layout regardless of the layout knob; when
+  `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_HOST_TABLE_DIR` holds a complete disk table for the layer, the loader skips
+  the checkpoint rows (`_load_rows` marks the table reused) and `finish_load` fills the memfd with
+  `_HostTable.fill_from_source`: this rank's byte range, `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED_THREADS`
+  (8) workers, 64 MiB `preadv` chunks straight into the mapping (page cache → shmem, no user
+  copy), then a TP barrier, then `cudaHostRegister` (flags 0 = mapped + portable under UVA, so the
+  host pointer is the device pointer). Without a complete disk table the loader writes the rows
+  from the checkpoint as before and the pin still happens after the fill.
+- Guard: before touching memory, rank 0 requires `MemAvailable ≥ table + SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED_RESERVE_GIB`
+  (16 GiB); the second table sees the first one's pages already charged. Size mismatch and short
+  reads raise. No silent fallback to the disk path.
+- Runtime: nothing new. With `backing_path` None the existing shared-layout path in
+  `EngramEmbedding.forward` runs `engram_gather` on the host pointer inside the captured graph
+  (decode, verify and extend alike), the pre-gather gate in `DeepseekV4Model` is off (it requires a
+  disk-backed table), so the pre-replay hook is a no-op and the hasher commits in-graph as in the
+  original design.
+- Partial pin was not built: the ids are hashes of n-gram windows over the compressed vocab, the
+  table is 2 × 384 M rows, and no hot subset was demonstrated; the whole table fits.
+
+## Test (`kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_engram_pinned.py`, SM120 image, GPU 1)
+
+1. Rows gathered from the pinned memfd are bitwise equal to the disk path (unique rows staged
+   to the device, same dequant kernel) for 4096 random ids with duplicates and for the first
+   65,536 rows.
+2. Capture/replay of the host-pointer gather with a static id buffer is bitwise equal to eager
+   for three random id sets.
+3. Registering charges no VRAM (0.00 MiB per GiB → 0 MiB for the two real tables).
+4. compute-sanitizer memcheck 0 errors, racecheck 0 hazards.
+
+Latency in isolation (warm kernel, cold rows, includes a 24/72-element id refresh per iteration):
+
+| rows | 0.25 GiB table | 4 GiB table |
+|---|---|---|
+| 24 | 4.1 µs | 4.8 µs |
+| 72 (M = 3) | 16.1 µs | 29.9 µs |
+| 1536 | 20.5 µs (19 GB/s) | 57 µs (6.9 GB/s) |
+| 98,304 (a 4096-token prefill chunk) | | 4.1 ms (6.2 GB/s) |
+
+Fill primitives (`scratchpad/engram-test/fill_test.py`, 1 GiB from a warm page cache): 6.6 GiB/s
+with one thread, 53 GiB/s with eight; `cudaHostRegister` 0.18 s per GiB.
+
+## Prediction
+
+Per step and rank at M = 1..3: remove ~289 µs of host time + the sync + the eager pre-replay
+launches for engram, add 2 in-graph gathers of ≤ 72 rows (≈ 2 × 5–30 µs). Expected: −0.25 to
+−0.35 ms of the 7.70 ms step (≈ +3–5 % single-stream), less at cc3 where the host work overlapped
+other streams. Boot: +~10 s fill per table (two ranks, page-cache source) + ~30 s register; RAM:
++189 GiB shmem (pinned, unevictable), the disk tables' page cache becomes droppable.
+
+## Measurement (A/B/A, frozen benchmark, 1M cc3, FP8 head + wo_a + fusion + PDL_ALL in every arm)
+
+Three frozen runs on 2026-09-11, bench_v41 n=3 × 512 tokens (server-log gen throughput means):
+
+| run | arm | single tok/s | cc3 tok/s | note |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 (22:20) | A disk pre-gather | **133.3** | **276.0** | page cache warm: no pinned boot yet |
+| 1 | B pinned copy | boot failed | | THP compaction stall, see below |
+| 2 (22:45) | A disk | 105.9 | 210.8 | after run 1's 150 GiB shmem evicted the disk tables' cache |
+| 2 | B pinned copy | **138.9** | **283.3** | GSM8K-100 nothink 99.0 %, GSM8K-20 think 95.0 % (19/20) |
+| 2 | A2 disk | 92.5 | 176.7 | cache evicted again by B |
+| 3 (23:00) | A disk, measured after "populated" | 116.1 | 263.1 | prewarm completed 131 s after boot |
+| 3 | B pinned copy | **138.7** | **281.4** | |
+| 3 | A2 disk, after "populated" | 97.5 | 173.6 | |
+
+B is stable across independent boots (138.9 / 138.7 single, 283.3 / 281.4 cc3, ±0.3 %). The disk
+baseline is not: every pinned boot allocates 189 GiB of shmem, which evicts the disk tables from the
+page cache, and the disk path's host gather (and its background MADV_POPULATE_READ prewarm) then
+runs against a cold or churning cache. The clean comparison is B against the run-1 baseline measured
+before any pinned boot: **+4.1 % single-stream (133.3 → 138.9), +2.0 % cc3 (276.0 → 281.4/283.3)**,
+which matches the prediction (−0.25 to −0.35 ms of a 7.70 ms step). Against a baseline that has
+just lost its cache the gap is 20–50 %, which is the operational argument: the pinned path does not
+depend on page-cache warmth at all.
+
+Deployed 23:19:30 on the benchmark server (1M cc3): `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED=copy` on top of
+GEMV, FP8 head, FP8 wo_a, launch fusion and, new to the deployed set, `SGLANG_DSV41_PDL_ALL=1`.
+
+### Boot-time and RAM deltas (per rank, measured)
+
+| | disk pre-gather | pinned copy |
+|---|---|---|
+| boot to /health | 82–105 s | 142–171 s |
+| fill per table (this rank's 47.2 GiB, both ranks concurrent, 16 threads, base pages) | | 17.8–25.7 s (1.8–2.7 GiB/s) |
+| cudaHostRegister per table | | 6.2–9.7 s (33 s once, under compaction load) |
+| host RAM | disk tables in page cache (reclaimable) | Shmem +189 GiB pinned: MemAvailable 405 → 203 GB |
+| VRAM | | 0 (registration charges no device memory) |
+
+Failure on the first attempt: with `MADV_HUGEPAGE` on the memfd (the shared-layout default), the
+fill faulted through direct compaction: table 1 took 83 s at 0.6 GiB/s for 29 % huge pages, table 2
+crawled at 0.04 GiB/s with `kcompactd` and `khugepaged` pegged, the boot passed the script's
+20-minute window and the A/B fell back to the baseline. Fix (commit bf84fba): base pages by default
+(`SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PINNED_THP=1` restores the advice), 16 fill threads, progress log every 8 GiB.
+Huge pages could not have helped: 72 random single-row reads per step span 72 distinct 2 MiB
+regions of a 94 GiB table either way.
+
+### nsys per step (49 decode steps, `profile/engram_on.sqlite`, vs `fusion_on.sqlite`)
+
+| | fusion + PDL (A) | pinned (B) |
+|---|---|---|
+| engram launches / step | 6 (hash, 2 gate, 3 fill-path) | 5 (hash, 2 gate, 2 in-graph gathers) |
+| in-graph gather | | 10.4 µs per layer (72 rows over PCIe) |
+| all-stream idle | 0.92 ms | 0.70 ms |
+| H2D copies per graph launch | 4.6 | 0.45 |
+| D2H copies per graph launch | 2.4 | 1.3 |
+| cudaEventSynchronize / cudaStreamSynchronize per graph launch | 3.1 / 1.6 | 1.0 / 0.5 |
+| launches / step | 1730 | 1749 |
+
+The engram host path (dedupe, staging, H2D, sync) is gone from the step; what remains of the idle
+is ~266 µs of Python between the eager pre-replay memset/copy nodes (attention metadata) plus the
+graph launch itself, the next item. The `cross_device_reduce_1stage` durations in these traces
+(0.41 vs 1.19 ms) are inter-rank arrival skew under node-level tracing (the profiled server ran at
+6 tok/s), not a property of either arm; the bench numbers above are the comparison.
+
+## Result
+
+Prediction −0.25 to −0.35 ms per step; measured −0.30 ms (+4.1 % single, +2.0 % cc3) against a warm
+baseline, exact by construction (same gather kernel, same bytes), sanitizer clean, GSM8K at parity.
+Cost: +60–70 s boot, 189 GiB of pinned host RAM. Commits c711f5c (feature + test), bf84fba (THP fix),
+this notes commit. Tools: `scratch-v41/smoke/ab_engram.sh`, `ab_engram2.sh` (prewarm-gated baselines),
+`scratchpad/engram-test/{reg_test,fill_test,fill_real}.py`.
