+# Block-FP8 GEMV for the bf16-at-decode linears (branch `dsv41-fp8-linears`)
+
+`SGLANG_DSV41_LINEARS_FP8_GEMV=1` (sites: `SGLANG_DSV41_LINEARS_FP8_GEMV_SITES`,
+default `wo_a`) serves the attention output absorb `wo_a` through a grouped variant
+of the SM120 streaming block-FP8 GEMV. Default off. Builds on `dsv41-fp8-lmhead`.
+
+## Attribution of the 44 cuBLAS gemvx launches per decode step
+
+From `profile/lmhead_on.sqlite` (1M cc3 config, FP8 head on, 49 traced decode steps at
+M = 1, one TP rank), by kernel signature, grid and position in the layer sequence:
+
+| launches/step | us/launch | us/step | kernel (cuBLAS gemvx signature, grid) | call site | weight per rank | why bf16 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 40 | 27.0 | 1058 | bf16 x bf16 -> bf16, fp32 acc, grid (256, 1, 4) | `torch.einsum("tgd,grd->tgr", o, wo_a)` in `DeepseekV4Attention.forward` (`_apply_wo_a_bf16_matmul`), right after `deepseek_rope_kernel` and before the `wo_b` GEMV [5120, 4096] | `wo_a` [4 groups x 1024, 4096] bf16 = 33.5 MB (checkpoint: `attn.wo_a.weight` e4m3 [8192, 4096] + `attn.wo_a.scale` e8m0 [256, 128]) | `wo_a_fp8_gemm_enabled` requires 128x128 block scales for DeepGEMM `fp8_einsum`; V4.1 ships [32, 32] blocks, so `_dequant_fp8_wo_a_streaming` dequantizes to bf16 at load and the aiter/TP4-Triton GEMV paths do not apply at TP2 |
+| 3 | 10.5 | 31 | bf16 x fp32 -> fp32, grid (256, 1, 1) | `F.linear(x_flat, hc_fn)` in the torch mHC pre path (`hc_pre_torch_impl`), between the RMSNorm and the next dense GEMV; only the layers that take the torch path | `hc_attn_fn` / `hc_ffn_fn` fp32 [24, 20480] = 2 MB | fp32 by design (mHC mixing weights); latency-bound, 2 MB |
+| 1 | 8.8 | 9 | bf16 x bf16 -> bf16, grid (128, 1, 1) | once per step at the first layer after the RMSNorm, before the [1792, 5120] GEMV | small (~4 MB) | not identified further; 9 us |
+
+Converted: `wo_a` (40/step, 1.06 ms). Left bf16/fp32 deliberately: the mHC `hc_*_fn`
+matmuls (fp32 mixing weights, 2 MB, precision-relevant, 31 us/step) and the single
+9 us launch.
+
+## Design
+
+- `kernels/jit/csrc/gemm/sm120_block_fp8_grouped_gemv.cuh`: the dense GEMV's warp-per-row
+  streaming loop with grid.y = groups; x rows are G*K apart, group g's weight rows start
+  at g*N, output rows are G*N apart; PDL wait/trigger inside, `enable_pdl` at launch.
+- `kernels/ops/gemm/sm120_block_fp8_grouped_gemv.py`: JIT wrapper + prebuild (same
+  buckets 1..32 as the dense GEMV).
+- `srt/layers/dsv41_linears_fp8.py`: `capture_wo_a_fp8` records the raw checkpoint
+  `wo_a.weight` (e4m3) and `wo_a.scale` (e8m0) per layer while the loader streams
+  (before the bf16 dequant), `install_wo_a_fp8_gemv` shards rows by `wo_a.tp_rank`,
+  converts the scales to fp32 (exact powers of two), prebuilds the buckets and frees the
+  bf16 param unless `_KEEP_BF16=1`; `wo_a_fp8_gemv` serves M <= `_MAX_M` (default 8)
+  through the grouped GEMV and larger M through the bf16 weight if kept, else a
+  dequant-on-the-fly einsum.
+- `srt/models/deepseek_v4.py`: capture hook in `load_weights`, install after the LM head
+  install, dispatch in the bf16 `else` branch of the absorb. The DSpark drafter
+  (`is_nextn`) is not converted.
+- Numerics: the bf16 dequant of e4m3 x 2^e is exact, so bf16 einsum and fp8 GEMV compute
+  the same products; only fp32 summation order differs.
+
