+# Block-FP8 LM head on the SM120 streaming GEMV (branch `dsv41-fp8-lmhead`)
+
+`SGLANG_DSV41_LMHEAD_FP8_GEMV=1` quantizes the bf16 LM head shard at load and serves
+decode logits through `sm120_block_fp8_gemv` (the dense-linear GEMV). Default off.
+
+## What the head is
+
+- Checkpoint `head.weight`: bf16 `[129280, 5120]`, `tie_word_embeddings: false`.
+- `ParallelLMHead` shards the vocab over TP: `[64640, 5120]` per rank at TP2 (padded to
+  64, no padding needed here), `quant_method` = `UnquantizedEmbeddingMethod`.
+- Callers: `LogitsProcessor._get_logits_impl` (decode: one row per running request;
+  prefill: last token per sequence unless logprobs over the prompt are requested) and
+  `dspark.project_through_lm_head` (DSpark draft/verify: up to block x bs rows, 24 on the
+  fast lane at cc4). Both take the new branch when `lm_head.dsv41_fp8_weight` is set.
+
+## Design
+
+- `srt/layers/dsv41_lm_head_fp8.py`: `quantize_block_fp8` (e4m3, fp32 `[N/32, K/32]`
+  scales = per-block amax / 448; the kernel multiplies by fp32 scales, so no ue8m0
+  rounding), `install_lm_head_fp8_gemv` (called from `DeepseekV4ForCausalLM.load_weights`
+  after `post_load_weights`; prebuilds all GEMV buckets; frees the bf16 shard unless
+  `_KEEP_BF16=1`, setting `lm_head.weight = None` so any bypassing reader fails loudly),
+  `lm_head_fp8_gemv` (M <= `_MAX_M` -> one GEMV launch; larger M -> bf16 matmul if the
+  shard was kept, else 32-row GEMV chunks).
+- Env: `SGLANG_DSV41_LMHEAD_FP8_GEMV`, `_MAX_M` (default 8), `_KEEP_BF16` (default off).
+- Memory per rank: +331 MB fp8 +1.3 MB scales, -662 MB bf16 when freed (net -330 MB).
+- Capture: the GEMV allocates its output with `torch.empty` inside the graph like the
+  dense path; captured decode graphs (bs 1..3) replay it. No PDL (the GEMV has none).
+
+## Measurements (RTX PRO 6000 x2, TP2, keep224m, 1M cc3 config, 2026-09-11)
+
+Isolated, real rank-0 shard (`kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_lm_head_fp8.py --rows 4096`):
+
+| M | bf16 cuBLAS | fp8 GEMV |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | 462 us (1434 GB/s) | 227 us (1460 GB/s) |
+| 3-8 | 464-487 us | 250 us |
+| 16 | 464 us | 490 us |
+| 24 | 471 us | 938 us |
+| 32 | 483 us | 1110 us |
+
+The GEMV halves the bytes and holds ~1.4 TB/s to M = 8; its per-byte fp32 FMAs make it
+level at M = 16 and 2x slower from M = 24 (hence `_MAX_M = 8`; a DSpark fast lane with
+cc4 verify batches should set `_KEEP_BF16=1` so M > 8 keeps the bf16 matmul).
+
+Numerics vs the production bf16 matmul on the shard (top-1 over the half vocab):
+
+| proxy hidden states | top-1 agree fp8 vs bf16 | KL(bf16 || fp8) mean / max | max dlogit | rel RMS err vs fp32: bf16 / fp8 |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| RMS-normed Gaussian x norm.weight | 93.8% | 4.0e-3 / 1.8e-2 | 0.59 (logit range 22.7) | 1.7e-3 / 2.6e-2 |
+| RMS-normed embed rows x norm.weight | 93.9% | 4.0e-3 / 1.5e-2 | 0.56 (range 32.4) | 1.7e-3 / 2.7e-2 |
+
+The proxies produce near-flat logits (many near-ties), so the 94% top-1 is a floor; the
+2.6% relative logit noise is the e4m3 mantissa (3 bits) averaged over K = 5120.
+
+In situ (same boot type, `bench_v41.py` n=3 x 512 tokens, and the server log's gen
+throughput; benchmark frozen during the A/B):
+
+| | bf16 head (flag off) | fp8 head (flag on) |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 stream | 86.1 tok/s (log 84.0) | 87.5 tok/s (log 85.4), +1.7% |
+| 3 streams | 192.0 tok/s (log 190.8) | 193.6 tok/s (log 192.7), +1.0% |
+| nsys per step at M=1: LM head | 1 cuBLAS gemvx, ~470 us | 1 GEMV, ~223 us |
+| nsys per step: dense GEMM (cublas gemvx) bucket | 45 launches, 1.590 ms | 44 launches, 1.118 ms |
+| GSM8K-100 nothink | 99% (prior baseline) | 100.0% |
+| GSM8K-20 think (max effort) | 97% (prior baseline, 100 q) | 95.0% |
+| greedy 20 prompts x 128 tokens vs flag off | | 1/20 identical; ON-vs-ON rerun also 1/20 (noise floor: cc3 batching is not run-to-run deterministic), divergence positions match |
+
+Correction to the earlier step breakdown: the "LM head 1.59 ms, 45 launches" figure in
+NOTES-flat-moe.md lumped every cuBLAS gemvx of the step into the head. The head is ONE
+gemvx launch of ~470 us; the other 44 launches (~25 us each, ~1.1 ms per step, 9%) are
+bf16 matmuls elsewhere in the layer stack and are the next candidate for the same
+treatment (find them by name in the nsys sqlite: `std::enable_if... gemvx`).
+
+Verdict: small, real win (+1.5-2% decode) at quality parity; swapped into the running
+Terminal-Bench 2.1 server at 20:43 (`v41 1m server up ... with SGLANG_DSV41_LMHEAD_FP8_GEMV=1`
+in `tb/jobs/tb21_launcher.log`).
+
+## Benchmark procedure
+
+```
+# isolated numerics + timing (needs the checkpoint; ~3 GB GPU)
+docker run --rm --gpus '"device=1"' -v $SRC:/sgl-workspace/sglang/python/sglang:ro \
+  -v /mnt/nvme-1/dsv41-sglang-jit:/root/.cache/sglang -v /home/ian/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash:/models/ckpt:ro \
+  local/sglang-dsv41:base python /sgl-workspace/sglang/python/sglang/kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_lm_head_fp8.py --rows 4096
+# in situ: boot the 1M cc3 config with EXTRA_ENV="-e SGLANG_DSV41_DECODE_DENSE_GEMV=1 -e SGLANG_DSV41_LMHEAD_FP8_GEMV=1",
+# then bench_v41.py --cc 1/3 --max-tokens 512 --n 3, gsm8k_eval.py --n 100 --mode nothink,
+# and NSYS_OUT=lmhead_on EXTRA_ENV="-e SGLANG_DSV41_LMHEAD_FP8_GEMV=1" smoke/nsys_cycle.sh + nsys export + smoke/nsys_steps.py.
+```
