@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Decode-step launch fusion and PDL (branch `dsv41-launch-fusion`)
+
+Target: the idle time of the captured decode step on the 1M cc3 config (keep224m, GEMV, FP8 LM
+head, FP8 wo_a), measured per rank at M = 1 from `profile/linears_on.sqlite`
+(nsys `--cuda-graph-trace=node -t cuda`): span 9.85 ms, kernel sum 8.97 ms, GPU-busy (union over
+streams) 7.18 ms, **all-stream idle 2.67 ms**, 1990 launches.
+
+Tools left behind (`scratch-v41/smoke/`):
+- `nsys_gaps.py file.sqlite [topN]`: per kernel name, launches/step, kernel µs/step, same-stream gap
+  before it, plus the all-stream idle charged to the kernel that ends each idle interval.
+- `nsys_idle.py file.sqlite [step] [threshold_us]`: every idle interval of one step with the
+  kernel/memcpy on both sides and the host runtime-API calls overlapping it, so idle is charged to
+  Python/CPU, `cudaGraphLaunch`, or a sync.
+- `nsys_steps.py` (per-step category breakdown), `nsys_cycle.sh` + `launch_prune_nsys.sh` (boot a
+  server under nsys and profile 48 decode tokens).
+
+## Where the 2.67 ms of idle per step was (baseline)
+
+| idle / step | what | evidence (`nsys_idle.py`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| ~1.8-2.0 ms (2 x ~0.9-1.2 ms) | Engram decode pre-gather, one interval per engram layer (1 and 14): between the `uniq.to("cpu")` D2H and the H2D of the gathered rows the host runs **858 µs of pure Python** with only 17 µs of CUDA API calls. Both tables are 100 % page-cache resident (mincore) and a random row costs 3.9 µs, so this is the `torch.unique` (6 GPU kernels + stream sync) + `ThreadPoolExecutor` gather (n threads for n ≤ 8 rows) + `arange` + `engram_gather` + `out_u[inverse]` + `copy_` + `zero_` chain, twice per step. | `874.7us [CPY s30] -> [CPY s30] API 17us; Python/CPU 858us` |
+| 205 µs | `cudaGraphLaunch` of the 1990-node decode graph: the GPU runs the first nodes and waits for the rest to be submitted (~0.10 µs per node). | `205.1us ... API 205us (cudaGraphLaunch)` |
+| ~150 µs | the eager pre-replay launches (attention metadata: `_page_table_positions_kernel`, `_causal_swa_page_indices_kernel`, 26 one-block `vectorized_elementwise` ops, copies; engram hash) and post-replay sampling ops: 30-40 µs windows of Python between launches. | intervals of 31-42 µs before `_page_table_positions_kernel`, `_engram_gather_kernel`, ... |
+| ~0.45 ms | per-node scheduling gaps inside the graph: 0.18-0.54 µs before each of ~1990 nodes (vectorized_elementwise 90 µs, CUTLASS MoE 35 µs, fused_k_norm_rope 31 µs, GEMV 16 µs, mHC 30 µs, allreduce 15 µs, ...). PDL can only act on this part. | `nsys_gaps.py` idle attribution |
+
+## Elementwise chains per layer (baseline, 477 elementwise launches / step, 509 µs GPU)
+
+| chain | launches / layer | µs / layer | site | action |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| prune top-k remap: `.to(long)` copy, `clamp`, `remap[safe]` gather, `< 0`, `full_like`, `where` | 6 (240 / step) | 6.1 (244 / step) | `PrunedExperts.remap_topk_ids` from `Mxfp4FlashinferCutlassMoEMethod.apply` | **deleted**: router gate rows + correction biases permuted once at the first forward so top-k emits slot ids (`router_remap` site) |
+| post-MoE combine add (5 blocks) | 1 (40) | 0.6 | shared-expert + routed output add | left (would need the CUTLASS finalize epilogue; 24 µs / step) |
+| pre-attention 1-block op | 1 (40) | 0.4 | attention metadata per layer | left (16 µs / step) |
+| side-stream ops (`index_elementwise`, `vectorized`, `direct_copy`, `alloc_decode`) on stream 70 | ~6 (240) | ~10 | overlap scheduler / next-batch metadata, overlapped with the MoE | left (not on the critical path) |
+| Engram layers 1 and 14: gate, elementwise x2 | 3 (6) | 3 | `_engram_gate_kernel` + scale/add | left |
+| pre-replay eager: 26 `vectorized_elementwise` (1 block) + copies + `arange` | 41 / step | 35 | attention metadata replay prep, engram hash | left in this pass (host time, ~150 µs idle; next candidate) |
+| post-replay eager: sampling, index ops | ~15 / step | 40 | sampler | left |
+
+## What was built
+
+1. **engram_fill** (`EngramEmbedding.fill_decode_pregather_cpu`, driver in
+   `DeepseekV4Model.engram_fill_decode_pregather`): one `hash_ids.to("cpu")` per step for all
+   engram layers (one stream sync instead of two), `np.unique` on the host, one `index_select` per
+   table into pinned staging, one H2D, one `engram_gather` that writes every (token, column) row
+   straight into the static pre-gather buffer using the inverse map. Per layer: 3 GPU ops (H2D,
+   gather, pad memset) instead of 12, no thread pool. Rows and dequant kernel are the same, so the
+   buffer is bit-identical (test 1). `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_FILL_TIMING=N` logs the host phases.
+2. **router_remap** (`_dsv41_apply_prune_router_mask`): gate weight rows and both correction
+   biases are permuted in place (kept experts first, in keep order, which is ascending, so ties
+   break in the same relative order), dropped rows get the -1e30 bias; `apply()` skips the remap
+   when `_dsv41_prune_permuted` is set. Exact: same logits in a new order (test 2, bitwise ids and
+   weights through `moe_fused_gate`). The expert-stats hook needs global ids and now raises if
+   enabled together with this site.
+3. **PDL on the dense GEMV** (`sm120_block_fp8_gemv.cuh`, template `kUsePDL`): the first k-step of
+   every row's weight and scale is loaded before `griddepcontrol.wait`, the trigger follows the
+   wait, then x is staged. Output bitwise identical to the plain build; capture/replay bitwise
+   (test 3). `SGLANG_DSV41_PDL_ALL=1` builds and launches the PDL variant (208 launches / step).
+
+Flags: `SGLANG_DSV41_FUSE_ELEMENTWISE=1`, `SGLANG_DSV41_FUSE_ELEMENTWISE_SITES=router_remap,engram_fill`
+(drop a site to disable it), `SGLANG_DSV41_PDL_ALL=1`.
+
+## Predictions (first principles) vs measurement (per step, per rank, M = 1, nsys)
+
+| item | launches | predicted saving | measured |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| engram_fill | -20 (2 x 6 unique + arange/gather/index/copy -> H2D + gather + memset) | 1.5-1.7 ms: two ~0.9 ms Python windows become one sync + ~100 µs host per layer (72 rows: dedupe+staging 36 µs, host gather 13 µs, H2D+launch 47 µs, logged) | idle windows 875+~900 µs -> 108 µs + 181 µs: **-1.6 ms** |
+| router_remap | -240 | 0.25-0.3 ms: 216 µs of serial remap kernels + ~50 µs node gaps + ~25 µs of graph launch (0.10 µs/node) | elementwise kernel time 254 -> 125 µs, graph launch 205 -> 188 µs, launches 1990 -> 1730: **~-0.2 ms** |
+| GEMV PDL | 0 | 0.1-0.2 ms: tail-wave overlap of 208 launches | GEMV kernel time 2631 -> 2579 µs; +1.1 % single-stream on top of fusion: **~-0.08 ms** |
+| total | -260 | ~2.0 ms | span 9.854 -> 7.702 ms (**-2.15 ms, -21.8 %**), all-stream idle 2.674 -> 0.919 ms |
+
+Remaining idle after (0.92 ms): engram fill 108 + 181 µs (one sync + Python), main graph launch
+188 µs (1730 nodes), metadata graph launch 42 µs, ~0.4 ms of per-node gaps on kernels that already
+carry PDL. Next candidates in order: fuse the 41 eager pre-replay metadata launches (host time),
+move the remaining engram host work off the critical path (needs the hash ids one step early or a
+pinned in-RAM table with an in-graph gather), and shrink the node count further (post-MoE add,
+per-layer attention-prep op) to cut the graph launch.
+
+## A/B/A on the 1M cc3 config (frozen 21:49-22:06, bench_v41 n=3 x 512 tokens; server-log gen throughput in parentheses)
+
+| arm | single-stream tok/s (rounds) | cc3 aggregate tok/s (rounds) |
+|---|---|---|
+| A baseline (FP8 head + wo_a) | 96.2 / 103.3 / 103.7 (101.6) | 224.3 / 228.1 / 226.2 (226.1) |
+| B fusion (router_remap + engram_fill) | 122.2 / 133.9 / 134.1 (131.9) | 270.9 / 279.1 / 275.6 (275.3) |
+| C fusion + PDL_ALL | 123.5 / 135.5 / 135.4 (133.4) | 274.0 / 278.3 / 275.0 (276.5) |
+| A2 baseline again | 97.2 / 103.6 / 103.8 (102.1) | 223.9 / 225.4 / 225.5 (224.7) |
+
+Baseline spread A vs A2: 0.4 % single, 0.6 % cc3 (same boot type, back to back). Fusion: **+28.5 %
+single, +22 % cc3** over the baseline mean; PDL adds +1.1 % single (above the spread, consistent in
+every round) and 0.4 % at cc3.
+
+Numerics: every site is exact by construction (tests bitwise); GSM8K-100 nothink 99.0 % on arm C
+(baseline 99-100 %), GSM8K-20 think on the deployed arm: see Result. compute-sanitizer on the PDL GEMV:
+memcheck 0 errors, racecheck 0 hazards.
+
+## PDL capability of the decode graph (SM120)
+
+| kernel family (launches / step) | PDL | how |
+|---|---|---|
+| dense block-FP8 GEMV (208) | **made capable** | `kUsePDL`: first weight/scale chunk prefetched before `griddepcontrol.wait`, trigger after the wait |
+| grouped GEMV wo_a (40), tiny router GEMM (40), rope / k-norm-rope (120), silu_mul_clamp (40), custom allreduce (80), JIT rmsnorm, topk, per-token quant | capable already | `kUsePDL = is_arch_support_pdl()` (major >= 9) in the JIT wrappers |
+| FlashInfer CUTLASS MoE (5 x 40), FlashInfer rmsnorm (121), sparse-MLA sm120 decode + merge (80) | capable already | `enable_pdl is None -> device_support_pdl()` (true on SM120) |
+| Triton mHC (4 x 40), `_router_triton_kernel` (40) | capable already | `launch_pdl=True` + `gdc_wait` / `gdc_launch_dependents` |
+| Triton page_mark / page_split (80), engram gate/hash, metadata kernels | incapable (as written) | no `launch_pdl`; 0.19 µs idle per launch, ~15 µs / step total |
+| torch elementwise / index / copy (169 after), cuBLAS gemvx (4), memcpy/memset nodes | incapable | no launch attribute; the remap chain (240) was deleted instead |
+| DeepGEMM indexer kernels | not checked | |
+
+Most of the graph already ran with PDL, which is why per-node gaps were only 0.18-0.54 µs and
+PDL_ALL is worth ~1 %: the dense GEMV was the one large family without it.
+
+## Result
+
+Deployed on the benchmark server at 22:06: `SGLANG_DSV41_FUSE_ELEMENTWISE=1` (both sites), PDL_ALL
+off (the A/B script's decision block hit a parsing bug and took the fusion-only branch; PDL_ALL is
+a measured +1.1 % single-stream and should be added at the next restart). GSM8K-20 think on the
+deployed server: 95.0 % (baseline 19/20 = 95 %). Commits: f17d834 (feature + tests + tools), docs
+commit ac54f16 and this one.
