+++ b/NOTES-replay-prep.md
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Decode-step host overhead and the post-top-k slot chain (branch `dsv41-replay-prep`)
+
+Target as assigned: "~266 µs per decode step of Python and eager launches around the graph
+replay" plus the cudaGraphLaunch cost, on the 1M cc3 config with the full deployed stack
+(GEMV, FP8 head, FP8 wo_a, launch fusion, PDL_ALL, pinned Engram).
+
+## 1. Attribution: the 266 µs did not exist
+
+`smoke/nsys_idle.py` (used for the earlier notes) took each step's kernels but added memcpy and
+memset events from 300 µs *before* the step's first kernel without the kernels that surround
+them, so the graph's own per-layer memset/memcpy nodes at the end of the previous step showed up
+as isolated events with 50-100 µs of "Python" between them. With every GPU activity (kernels,
+memcpy, memset; graph and eager; all streams) taken over the same window (`smoke/nsys_stepidle.py`,
+new), the pinned-Engram profile (`profile/engram_on.sqlite`, cc1, M=1) gives per rank:
+
+| quantity | rank 0 | rank 1 |
+|---|---|---|
+| graph span per step | 6.92 ms | 6.92 ms |
+| inter-graph GPU idle (last node of graph k to first node of graph k+1) | 0.0 µs | 0.0 µs |
+| in-graph idle, sum of all sub-node gaps | 153 µs (2.2%) | 149 µs (2.2%) |
+| cudaGraphLaunch host time | 249 µs | 247 µs |
+| graph nodes per step | 1792 (1705 kernels, 47 memcpy, 40 memset) | same |
+
+The host is never on the critical path: the scheduler runs one batch ahead, the next
+cudaGraphLaunch is issued 0-11 µs *before* the previous graph's last node ends, and the next
+graph's first node starts within 0.2 µs of it. The 248 µs launch call overlaps GPU execution.
+The eager pre-replay work (attention-metadata prep, sampler, D2H) runs inside the previous
+graph's span. `nsys_idle.py` is fixed (window = the step's own kernels) and now reports 0 idle.
+
+For the record, the pre-pinned profile (`fusion_on.sqlite`) had 471-477 µs of *real*
+inter-graph idle per step; that was the Engram host fill, which the pinned table removed.
+
+## 2. What is actually left inside the step
+
+In-graph idle of ~150 µs per step is the sum of ~1790 node-scheduling gaps of 0.05-0.2 µs; the
+largest groups sit after the 160 `vectorized_elementwise` nodes (30 µs), the 80 custom-allreduce
+nodes (15 µs) and the 80 mHC post-split nodes (15 µs). Only node removal reduces it.
+
+Per-layer node sequence (`profile/engram_on.sqlite`, layer 20, 67 nodes): the one chain of
+torch launches on the critical path is the decode indexer's post-top-k slot arithmetic in
+`_low_ratio_index_topk_decode` (`deepseek_v4_backend.py`), run by the five candidate-consuming
+layers per step (index source layers 24/28/32/36 plus the ratio-2 consumer): after
+`topk_transform_paged_v2` writes the raw selections, `mask_topk_scores` (gather, two compares,
+and, compare, not, masked_fill) then `clamp_min`, `//`, `%`, page-table `gather`, `*`, `+`,
+`>=`, `where`, and two `copy_` = 18 launches, 24.1 µs wall per layer, 121 µs per step (1.7% of
+the step), all on the attention stream so the sparse-MLA kernel waits for them.
+
+The cudaGraphLaunch cost curve from the saved profiles is linear in node count, ~0.14 µs per
+node: 2030 nodes 276-298 µs, 1870 nodes 275 µs, 1790 nodes 249-251 µs. Removing 85 nodes saves
+~12 µs of host time per step, which is overlapped anyway; node-priority instantiation and
+graph upload cannot move a launch that is not on the critical path, so they were not pursued.
+
+## 3. What was built
+
+`kernels/ops/attention/dsv4/topk_slots.py`: `topk_page_slots(selected, logits, page_table,
+page_size, page_indices, raw_indices=None, enable_pdl=None)`, one Triton program per batch row
+(`BLOCK = next_pow2(K)`, K = `index_topk` = 512), doing the same integer arithmetic as the chain
+and writing `page_indices` (and `raw_indices` when the metadata allocates it) in place.
+Exact by construction: integer ops and comparisons only; the score gather reads the same fp32
+values; `-1` padding, out-of-range columns and `-inf` scores map exactly as `mask_topk_scores`.
+PDL: `gdc_wait` before the first load, `gdc_launch_dependents` before the stores, launched with
+`launch_pdl` when `is_arch_support_pdl()` (SM120: yes). Wired in
+`DSV4AttnBackend._low_ratio_index_topk_decode` behind `SGLANG_DSV41_FUSE_TOPK_SLOTS=1`
+(`srt/environ.py`, default off); the torch chain stays as the reference path. Loud shape and
+dtype checks, no fallback.
+
+Verification (`kernels/jit/tests/test_dsv41_topk_slots.py`, dev container, GPU 1): bitwise
+equal to the torch chain over bs 1-4, L in {1, 63, 64, 65, 700, 4096, 16384}, 20% `-1` pads, 3%
+out-of-range selections, 15% `-inf` columns, PDL on and off; all-pad and all-`-inf` rows;
+capture/replay inside a CUDA graph with new inputs copied in, bitwise. compute-sanitizer
+memcheck 0 errors, racecheck 0 hazards (`kdev/san_topk.py`).
+
+Isolated, graph-replayed, 20 chains per graph (`kdev/bench_topk.py`): torch chain 56.5 µs (bs 1)
+/ 59.5 µs (bs 3) per chain; fused 1.2 / 1.3 µs; fused + PDL 1.0 / 1.1 µs.
+
+Prediction for the step: 5 layers x (24.1 - ~1.5) µs = ~110 µs per step, i.e. ~1.6% at cc1
+(6.9 ms step); the same absolute saving at cc3.
+
+## 4. Measurement (frozen A/B/A, 23:46-00:07, `smoke/ab_topk.sh`, `profile/ab_topk.log`)
+
+1M cc3 config, every arm with the deployed stack (GEMV, FP8 head, FP8 wo_a, launch fusion,
+PDL_ALL, pinned Engram); B adds `SGLANG_DSV41_FUSE_TOPK_SLOTS=1`. bench_v41 n=3 x 512 tokens
+(mean of the three rounds, round 0 is the cold one) and the server-log gen throughput.
+
