+# Engram decode pre-gather (SM120, disk-backed shared host table)
+
+## Problem
+
+On SM120 with the 189 GiB engram tables on an NVMe file (`SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_HOST_TABLE_DIR`,
+mapped `MAP_SHARED`), the captured decode CUDA graph runs the in-graph raw-pointer
+`engram_gather` (HMM path, taken because `is_current_stream_capturing()` is true during
+capture). On replay with fresh token ids it faults cold file pages into GPU page tables at
+~0.25–1 ms/row and does not stay resident — profiled as `_engram_gather_kernel` at 579 ms /
+24 calls (2 engram layers × 12 decode steps).
+
+Eager (extend/verify/uncaptured-decode) lookups already avoid this via `_disk_gather`
+(CPU `index_select` from the page cache → pinned staging ring → H2D → `engram_gather` on
+compact contiguous device rows). This change extends that to the captured decode graph.
+
+## Design
+
+Engram decode lookup ids depend only on the input token ids and the per-request n-gram
+history, both known on the host before the graph is replayed. So:
+
+- Before each decode replay, compute the hash ids eagerly (**`commit=False`**) and run the
+  existing `_disk_gather` into a **per-layer static device buffer** that the captured graph
+  reads. No in-graph HMM gather happens on replay.
+- The in-graph hasher still runs during replay and owns the single per-step history commit
+  (`commit=True`), reading the same pre-step history the eager pass read — so the eager ids
+  equal the in-graph ids and the buffered rows are bit-exact with the in-graph gather.
+- EXTEND / target-verify / DP-collective paths are untouched: the static-buffer branch is
+  taken only while capturing a **decode** graph on a disk-backed **shared** table.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- **`sglang/srt/environ.py`** — new `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_DECODE_PREGATHER = EnvBool(True)`.
+  Default-on, but only reaches effect behind the model gate below (SM120 + disk-backed shared
+  table), so "default on when disk-backed" holds. Set to `0` to disable.
+
+- **`sglang/srt/layers/engram.py`**
+  - `EngramHasher.forward(..., commit: bool = True)` — `commit=False` returns the ids without
+    writing history (the `if commit and commit_rows is not None:` guard). Existing callers pass
+    nothing → unchanged.
+  - `EngramEmbedding._init_host_table` — initializes `self._pregather_emb = None`.
+  - `EngramEmbedding.forward` — in the `_shared` + disk-backed branch, when capturing a decode
+    graph (`is_current_stream_capturing()` and `forward_batch.forward_mode.is_decode()`) and the
+    buffer is allocated, returns `self._pregather_emb[: indices.shape[0]]` instead of recording
+    `engram_gather`. Non-capturing decode still returns `_disk_gather`; capturing extend/verify
+    still record the in-graph `engram_gather`.
+  - `EngramEmbedding.enable_decode_pregather(capacity, n_hash_cols, device)` — allocates the
+    zero-initialized static bf16 buffer `[capacity, n_hash_cols, head_dim]` (idempotent; grows
+    only). Must run before capture so the captured read address is stable.
+  - `EngramEmbedding.fill_decode_pregather(indices)` — `buf[:t] = _disk_gather(indices)`;
+    `buf[t:].zero_()` for graph-padding rows.
+
+- **`sglang/srt/models/deepseek_v4.py`**
+  - `DeepseekV4Model.__init__` — computes `self._engram_decode_pregather_on` (gate:
+    `_is_cuda and is_sm120_supported()` + hasher present + single PP + `hc_pre_from_prev_sublayer`
+    + every engram layer `_shared` and disk-backed + env flag). Adds `and not
+    self._engram_decode_pregather_on` to the BS=1 KV-prefetch gate — the two are mutually
+    exclusive (pre-gather eliminates the fault that prefetch only overlaps, and covers all
+    engram layers, not just layer 14).
+  - `DeepseekV4Model.engram_setup_decode_pregather(capacity)` — allocate per-layer buffers.
+  - `DeepseekV4Model.engram_fill_decode_pregather(forward_batch)` — eager `commit=False` hash,
+    then fill each layer's buffer. No-op unless the gate is on and the mode is decode.
+  - `DeepseekV4ForCausalLM` — thin delegating `engram_setup_decode_pregather` /
+    `engram_fill_decode_pregather` (the runner sees the top-level model).
+
+- **`sglang/srt/model_executor/runner/decode_cuda_graph_runner.py`**
+  - `capture()` — before the capture loop, `engram_setup_decode_pregather(self.max_num_token)`
+    via `getattr` (no-op for other models / gated-off).
+  - `execute()` — between `load_batch` and `backend.replay`, `engram_fill_decode_pregather(
+    forward_batch)` via `getattr`. Runs on the current stream, so the fill is ordered before
+    the captured graph's reads on replay (same ordering the static input-id buffers rely on).
+
+## Enabling / disabling
+
+Automatic when the engram host table is disk-backed (`SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_HOST_TABLE_DIR` set,
+forcing the shared layout) **and** running on SM120. No new flag needs to be set. To force off:
+`SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_DECODE_PREGATHER=0`. Boot log confirms: `Engram decode pre-gather enabled
+for N disk-backed layer(s)`. When on, the BS=1 KV-prefetch (`SGLANG_ENABLE_DSV41_ENGRAM_KV_PREFETCH`)
+is automatically suppressed.
+
+## Target-verify (DSpark speculative decoding) extension
+
+The target-verify CUDA graph is captured by the **same** `DecodeCudaGraphRunner` class (a
+separate instance with `capture_forward_mode = TARGET_VERIFY`, `num_tokens_per_req = draft
+tokens`), so the runner hooks already fired for it; the original version only honoured
+`is_decode()`, leaving the verify graph on the in-graph HMM gather for every verify token
+(4 tokens × 48 rows × 2 layers per step ≈ the observed 9–12 tok/s).
+
+- **Per-mode static buffers.** `EngramEmbedding._pregather_emb` is now a dict keyed by
+  `pregather_mode_key(forward_mode)` → `"decode"` / `"verify"`. Each runner sizes its own
+  mode once (`max_bs` vs `max_bs × num_tokens_per_req`) before its capture. A captured read
+  bakes the buffer address, so one shared buffer could not grow for the second runner without
+  breaking the first runner's graphs.
+- **History semantics under target-verify (found in `EngramHasher.forward`):** MODE_VERIFY sets
+  `commit_rows = commit_last = None`, so the in-graph hasher **never commits in-forward**.
+  Predecessors come from the pre-verify history plus the in-batch draft block. After
+  acceptance, `dspark_worker_v2` → `NgramEmbeddingManager.update_after_verify` →
+  `EngramHasher.commit_after_verify(verify_ids_2d, req_pool_indices, commit_lens)` commits only
+  the accepted prefix (last `n-1` of `history ++ verify_ids` at `commit_lens`), so rejected draft
+  tokens never enter history. Therefore the eager `commit=False` hash reads exactly the state
+  the in-graph hasher reads, and the buffered rows are bit-exact with the in-graph gather.
+- **Drafter:** the DSpark draft models (`srt/models/dspark.py`, `deepseek_v4_dspark.py`) contain
+  no Engram, and draft runners have no hasher, so their hooks are gated off — only the target
+  model's verify graph needed the pre-gather.
+- The runner passes `self.capture_forward_mode` to `engram_setup_decode_pregather(capacity,
+  forward_mode)`; the fill derives the mode from `forward_batch.forward_mode`.
+
+## Host-side gather + prewarm timing (deep-prefill fix)
+
+Profiled 4096-token prefill chunks at depth 153K spent ~390 ms/chunk GPU-idle inside
+`_disk_gather`: the `index_select` over the file mmap took 315–333 ms for ~16.8K unique rows per
+layer (7.5–11 µs/row = page-fault bound), because (a) residency was only ~85–87% — the pread
+prewarm started at construction and lost the page-cache LRU race to the ~280 GiB checkpoint
+stream; (b) `MADV_RANDOM` keeps base pages; (c) `torch.set_num_threads(1)` after load serialised
+the ~2.5K major faults per layer per chunk. Cost is depth-independent (diverse text ~6.5K tok/s vs
+13–15K for repetitive text with few unique n-grams).
+
+- **`_HostTable.populate()`** (`srt/layers/engram.py`) — `madvise(MADV_POPULATE_READ = 22)` via
+  ctypes over the mapping's base pointer `self.bytes.data_ptr()` (`self.bytes` is the
+  `torch.frombuffer` uint8 view of `self.mm`) and `self.nbytes`. Faults every page into the page
+  cache **and this process's page tables** in one kernel pass (Linux ≥ 5.14). Returns `False`
+  after a warning with errno/strerror so the caller falls back to the pread prewarm.
+- **Prewarm trigger moved** from `_init_host_table` (construction, before weight loading) to
+  **`EngramEmbedding.finish_load`** (after every rank has written its rows), still behind
+  `SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_PREWARM`. `_start_prewarm` now runs `populate()` on **every rank** in a
+  daemon thread (each process maps its own page tables; the page-cache fill is shared); only rank 0
+  falls back to the sequential pread (which only fills the shared page cache). `EngramEmbedding`
+  now stores `self.layer_id` so `finish_load` can name the thread/log.
+- **Parallel gather** — `_disk_gather` no longer builds intermediate `w`/`sc` tensors and copies
+  them; `_gather_rows_into(ids, w_out, s_out)` runs `torch.index_select(..., out=view)` straight
+  into row-slices of the pinned staging views (`buf[:wb].view(n, dim)` / `buf[wb:need].view(n,
+  dim//32)`), split over **`SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_GATHER_THREADS = EnvInt(16)`** threads on a lazily
+  built per-layer `ThreadPoolExecutor` (`self._gather_pool`). `index_select` releases the GIL, so K
+  page faults proceed concurrently, sidestepping the single intra-op thread. `1` restores the
+  original single `index_select`. Every row is written exactly once from the same source row, so
+  the bytes are bit-identical (validated, Part 5). Slices are `(i·n//k, (i+1)·n//k)` with
+  `k = min(K, n)`; `n ≤ 1` takes the single path.
+- `MADV_RANDOM` was left as is (not in the requested fix; with `POPULATE_READ` doing the fill,
+  readahead no longer matters). The decode/verify pre-gather logic is untouched.
+
+## Scope / unchanged paths
+
+- EXTEND/prefill and uncaptured (eager) decode/verify are unchanged.
+- Non-disk-backed host tables and device-resident sharded tables are unchanged.
+- Breakable / piecewise (tc) decode graphs are not targeted here; this covers the full-capture
+  decode runner (`decode_cuda_graph_runner.py`) where the 24 ms was measured.
+
+## Validation
+
+`engram_decode_pregather_validation.py` (CPU-only; the two SM120 GPUs run a live server):
+
+1. Static-buffer round-trip is **bit-exact** with the in-graph gather. Writes a tiny fp8_e4m3 +
+   e8m0 table to a real file in the `_HostTable` byte layout, maps it, reproduces `_disk_gather`
+   (uint8 `index_select` → fp8 reinterpret → unique/inverse dequant — the arithmetic
+   `bf16(fp32(row) * 2**(exp-127))` that `engram_gather`'s kernel docstring specifies), stores
+   into the static buffer, and checks the sliced read equals a direct reference gather and that
+   the padding rows are zero, across decode token counts {48, 1, 200, 96}.
+2. `commit=False` ids equal the in-graph (`commit=True`) ids and leave history untouched across a
+   6-step decode, while the in-graph pass commits history each step — the invariant that makes the
+   pre-gathered rows match what the in-graph hasher would have looked up.
+3. **Target-verify:** ports the MODE_VERIFY predecessor logic and `commit_after_verify`; across a
+   5-step verify with random `commit_lens`, eager `commit=False` ids equal the in-graph ids, neither
+   pass commits in-forward, and the post-acceptance commit advances history by exactly the accepted
+   prefix (a rejected draft never becomes the newest entry).
+4. **Per-mode buffers:** the decode and verify buffers are distinct storage, address-stable on
+   re-setup, and filling one leaves the other untouched.
+5. **Sliced host gather:** a verbatim port of `_gather_rows_into` over a 20K-row synthetic uint8
+   table, for threads ∈ {1, 3, 16} and n ∈ {0, 1, 5, 16, 33, 257, 16843} (n < K, n == K,
+   n % K ≠ 0, ~the real 16.8K unique rows), writing via `index_select(..., out=)` into row-slices of
+   a flat staging buffer: bytes bit-identical to a single `index_select`, weight-then-scale flat
+   layout correct, no overrun past `need` (canary), slices tile `[0, n)` exactly, and the staged
+   bytes dequantize to the reference gather.
+
+Output: `engram_decode_pregather_validation_output.txt` — OVERALL: PASS.
+
+Upstream commit `86c55d7` already verified `_disk_gather` is bit-exact vs the in-graph
+`engram_gather` on GPU; the pre-gather only stores that verified result into a static buffer and
+slices it (a pure copy), which Part 1 confirms is identity.
