+++ b/sglang/NOTES-dsv41-expert-stream.md
@@ -0,0 +1,503 @@
+# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash zero-CPU-compute expert streaming (SM120, 2x RTX PRO 6000)
+
+Goal: run all 269 GiB of routed FP4 experts on the GPU while only ~190 GiB VRAM
+exists, with **zero CPU compute**. Experts stream to the GPU at runtime from
+**file-backed NVMe mmaps read over HMM**, so their resident cost is reclaimable
+page cache (not anonymous RSS — that OOMs) and all math stays on the GPU in the
+SM120 FlashInfer CUTLASS MXFP4 kernel.
+
+## What was built (design decision: option b)
+
+The SGLang GGUF `expert_pack` runtime is gated to `deepseek_v4` / TP1 / GGUF and
+would need a full rewrite for V4.1 (HF safetensors, `deepseek_v41`, TP2). The
+MXFP4 CUTLASS method already loads the real checkpoint, already computes experts
+from host memory over HMM device-views (the `SGLANG_DSV41_UVA_EXPERT_LAYERS`
+path), and is already wired. Its only failure was that the host staging was
+**anonymous** memory, which OOMs. So the minimal correct path was: **replace the
+anonymous host staging with a prebuilt file-backed mmap**, reusing the CUTLASS
