+# VRAM hot-expert cache (coalesced DMA staging + LRU persistence)
+
+Reading experts straight from the mmap via HMM is fault-driven and scattered
+(~8-9 tok/s, GPU util 0-27%). `ExpertCache` (in `mxfp4_expert_store.py`) adds a
+bounded VRAM pool of `S` expert slots per streamed layer, backed by the mmap
+pack, so the kernel reads HBM instead of faulting.
+
+## Mechanism
+- **Pool**: four real HBM tensors per streamed layer (`w13/w2` weights +
+  interleaved scales), shape `[S, ...]`, set as the layer's kernel params.
+- **Coalesced staging**: before a layer's MoE, `ensure_resident` finds the
+  routed experts not in the pool and copies their rows mmap->slot with a real
+  `cudaMemcpyAsync` on a dedicated copy stream (coalesced DMA, not fault-driven).
+  The copy stream waits for the prior kernel (WAR hazard) and the compute stream
+  then waits for the copy.
+- **Expert-id remap**: the SM120 CUTLASS kernel takes global topk ids and
+  filters by `ep_rank`/`num_local_experts` (= pool rows `S`). A resident global
+  expert `g` is remapped to `ep_rank*S + slot`; everything else to a skip id
+  `>= ep_size*S` the kernel drops. `topk_ids` are remapped in `apply()` via a
+  cached `[num_experts_total]` gather table (rebuilt only when residency
+  changes). At `S == num_local_experts` with in-order slots this is the identity
+  map, i.e. the plain resident path.
+
+## Eviction policy
+LRU (`OrderedDict`). Each call first moves its already-resident routed experts
+to the MRU end, so a miss's eviction can only reclaim a slot holding an expert
+**not** routed this call (never one the same kernel invocation still needs);
+newly staged experts are inserted at MRU too. Pre-population (`prewarm`) loads
+the profiled hot set at load: the explicit warm-set file if given, else the
+top-`S` local experts by hit count from the stats dir, else lazy fill. `stats`
+tracks hit/miss/evict.
+
+## Env knobs
+- `SGLANG_DSV41_EXPERT_CACHE_PER_LAYER` — `S` VRAM slots per streamed layer.
+  Unset => no cache (HMM mmap path). `full` or `>= num_local` => full pool
+  (identity, = resident). A smaller value exploits the routing skew.
+- `SGLANG_DSV41_EXPERT_CACHE_WARM_SET` — JSON `{layer_idx: [global_expert_id,...]}`
+  pre-staged at load.
+- `SGLANG_DSV41_EXPERT_STATS_DIR` — fallback warm set: top-`S` by hit count from
+  `<dir>/<prefix>.rank<r>.pt` (the counters the apply path already logs).
+
+## Correctness (RAN, PASSED)
+`test/srt/models/test_dsv41_expert_cache.py`, real layer-0 experts, 12
+single-token forwards that force staging + eviction, bit-exact vs the full
+`[E,...]` CUTLASS path:
