+# Prefill overflow fallback + TP-sharded packs
+
+## Prefill overflow (boot blocker, fixed)
+A prefill chunk (thousands of tokens x top-6) routes far more experts in one MoE
+call than the pool holds, so `ensure_resident` used to raise. Now, when a call's
+routed experts exceed the pool slots, `apply()` runs `_run_overflow`: the kernel
+reads ALL local experts from the mmap via HMM device-views (`full_device_views()`,
+the pre-cache path) with the unmodified global topk ids, for that call only.
+Decode calls (<= slots) keep the fast pool. One-time per-prompt cost; per-token
+decode stays cached. Bit-exact vs the full path (test: 16 experts routed, S=6).
+
+## TP-sharded packs (capacity for a big cache)
+`prepare_v41_expert_pack.py --shard-mode tp` writes, per TP rank, ALL experts
+column-sharded exactly as the TP loader splits them: w13 (gate_up) sharded on the
+intermediate/output dim, w2 (down) on the packed input dim, scales split the same
+way then block-interleaved on the shard. At world=2 each expert is half width
+(8.96 MiB): `w13[384,2304,2560] w2[384,5120,576]` + half-size scales, 3.36 GiB/
+layer/rank. The pack header records `num_experts_total=384`, `expert_lo=0`,
+`expert_hi=384`.
+
+The cache is parallel-mode agnostic: `_install_expert_cache` takes the kernel's
+EP topology from the layer (`moe_ep_rank`/`moe_ep_size`), not the pack's world.
+- EP pack: `expert_lo=ep_rank*192`, `num_local=192`, `moe_ep_size=2` -> remap id
+  `ep_rank*S + slot`, skip `2S`.
+- TP pack: `expert_lo=0`, `num_local=384`, `moe_ep_size=1`, `moe_tp_size=2`
+  handles the column shard -> remap id `slot`, skip `S`. Cache covers the global
+  384 experts directly, so `S=128` = the measured global top-128 (78% hit) at
+  `128 x 8.96 MiB x 20 layers = ~22 GiB/rank`.
+`_install_expert_cache` fails loud if the pack's per-expert shape does not match
+the params the method created for the running parallel config (wrong shard-mode).
+
+### Correctness (RAN, PASSED)
+`test/srt/models/test_dsv41_expert_cache.py`:
+```
+S=16 (identity)  : OK (bit-exact, 12 forwards)
+S= 8 / S= 6      : OK (bit-exact through eviction)
+overflow S=6     : OK (16 experts routed -> full HMM fallback == full path)
+TP shard sum vs full (allclose): OK  rel=3.6e-3  w13(16,2304,2560) w2(16,5120,576)
+```
+TP is a different numeric reduction than the full GEMM, so the two column-shards
+summed match the full MoE to allclose (rel 3.6e-3), not bit-exact; the pool path
+over a TP shard is separately bit-exact. A real TP pack round-trips through the
+store (header `num_experts_total=384`), and the cache builds a `[128,2304,2560]`
+pool = ~22 GiB/rank for 20 layers.
+
+## Launch recipes
+EP (current pack, small cache to fit):
+```
