+# Expert PRUNE mode (fully-resident, no streaming)
+
+Decision: drop the cold routed experts and keep the top-224/384 per layer fully
+resident in VRAM (fast, no mmap/HMM). Vision encoder, attention, dense, shared
+experts (FP8, separate), Engram (disk mmap) and DSpark are untouched — only
+routed MoE experts are pruned. Independent of the streaming pack/cache/UVA.
+
+## Mechanism (reuses the normal load/process/kernel path)
+`SGLANG_DSV41_EXPERT_KEEP_SET=/path.json` ({layer_idx: [kept global ids]}).
+1. LOAD ONLY KEPT: `create_weights` resizes the four expert params from 384 to
+   num_kept (224) and overrides the FusedMoE `_map_global_expert_id_to_local_expert_id`
+   so a kept global id maps to its slot and a dropped id returns -1 (the loader
+   already skips -1). So only kept experts occupy VRAM; `process_weights_after_loading`
+   runs unchanged on the 224 experts. All resident — no pack, no mmap, no HMM.
+2. ROUTER MASK (the crux): `scores_for_choice = sqrtsoftplus(logits) + correction_bias`,
+   so masking raw logits is unsafe (the bias is added after scoring). Instead, at
+   the first MoE forward, `_dsv41_apply_prune_router_mask` sets the dropped experts'
+   `e_score_correction_bias` AND `e_score_correction_bias_vl` to -1e30 (once, in
+   place). This excludes them from top-k for both text (`self.topk`) and vision
+   (`vision_topk`, `moe_fused_gate`) across every forward path.
+3. REMAP: `apply()` remaps the selected global ids to kept-slot ids (static
+   `remap` table) so the [num_kept,...] kernel weights are indexed correctly. The
+   router mask guarantees only kept ids are ever selected.
+
+Gated off by default (env unset). TP-only (fails loud under `--ep-size`; the
+keep-slot map holds the global kept set on every rank). Fails loud on fused
+shared experts (separate FP8 module here, so 0).
+
+## Correctness (RAN, PASSED, <2 GiB GPU, real layer-0 experts)
+`test/srt/models/test_dsv41_expert_prune.py`:
+```
+pruned MoE vs full-restricted (10/16 kept), 12 forwards: OK bit-exact
+router mask (256 tokens x top-6): OK, 0 dropped selected
+```
+The pruned [num_kept,...] MoE is bit-identical to the full tensor restricted to
+the kept experts (given routing hits only kept), and the masked bias never lets a
+dropped expert into top-k. Full-forward coherence is the coordinator's A/B.
+
+## Launch recipe (TP2, fully resident)
+```
+# keep set staged at /home/ian/models/dsv41-keep224.json (mount into container)
+--tp 2                          # NO --ep-size (prune is TP-only)
+--mem-fraction-static 0.90 --context-length 65536
+SGLANG_DSV41_EXPERT_KEEP_SET=/models/dsv41-keep224.json
+# leave the engram envs as-is (disk mmap); do NOT set the pack/UVA envs
+SGLANG_ENABLE_DSV41_ENGRAM_HOST_TABLE=1  SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_HOST_TABLE_DIR=/engram
+```
+CUDA graphs: prune adds only a static device-side remap gather in apply() and a
+one-time bias mask (applied at the first warmup forward, before capture), so
+graphs should work — try with graphs ON after a correct eager run (no staging
+syncs like the streaming path had).
+
+Sizing: 224 experts x 40 layers x 8.96 MiB (TP2 half-expert) = ~80 GiB/rank
+resident + dense/embed/vision ~10 + KV. Tight at mem-frac 0.90 on 95 GiB; if it
+OOMs, lower the keep count (regenerate the keep-set JSON with fewer ids) or the
+context length. Expected ~13% worst-layer routing mass dropped (86.7% kept);
+the user accepts the quality hit.
